From 77ae705eb5d2257ed3ee9163ec67a04003bfa8d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:08:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] LibGfx+LibWeb: Port to the Skia m148 path, gradient and
 span APIs

Skia m148 removes several APIs that Ladybird uses:

- SkPath lost all of its editing methods (moveTo, lineTo, arcTo, addPath,
  offset, transform, ...) and SkPath::ArcSize; paths are built with
  SkPathBuilder. PathImplSkia now keeps an SkPathBuilder and a cached
  immutable SkPath, which is dropped on every edit and snapshotted again
  on the next read. Copies start with the cache filled, so a copy handed
  to another thread is never written to by a read.
- SkFont::getPath(SkGlyphID, SkPath*) is gone; use the std::optional
  overload. SkTextUtils::GetPath() still replaces its output path, so
  text() keeps assigning the whole path as before.
- SkGradientShader is replaced by SkGradient and the SkShaders::*Gradient
  factories, which only take SkColor4f. Gradients that used SkColor now
  convert with to_skia_color4f(), which is exact, and keep the default
  interpolation (the old flags value of 0).
- SK_SUPPORT_UNSPANNED_APIS no longer exists; pass SkSpans to
  SkDashPathEffect::Make() and SkFont::textToGlyphs(), and use
  SkFont::getWidth() for a single glyph.

The path and span changes also build against m144; the gradient API is
m148 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
